1
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:16,800
The press conference for the launch of
The Memory The Series.

2
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:18,360
Why do we not know about any of this?

3
00:00:19,320 --> 00:00:20,760
Just walk away from the Dream!

4
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:23,720
It’s for the safety of the people around you.

5
00:00:24,560 --> 00:00:26,920
If you want revenge so badly,take it out on yourself.

6
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,680
but it will cause trouble for people around you as well.

7
00:00:31,320 --> 00:00:32,240
What are you going to do?

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,560
I came.

9
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,160
Now you guys can let him go.

10
00:01:35,520 --> 00:01:36,360
Sky?

11
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:41,200
You just came? I heard that you’ve been calling for us.

12
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:43,880
I'll hurry and get you the money.

13
00:01:45,960 --> 00:01:48,120
You already got me the money.

14
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:55,160
I'm sorry.

15
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:00,640
I'm really sorry.

16
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:02,760
I'm sorry.

17
00:02:05,360 --> 00:02:07,280
How's it been, trying to take your revenge?

18
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,520
Feeling any better?

19
00:02:18,720 --> 00:02:20,079
It's not what you think, is it?

20
00:02:20,800 --> 00:02:21,400
So...

21
00:02:22,440 --> 00:02:23,280
I think…

22
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:27,160
You can stop running after me, and Mom now.

23
00:02:35,160 --> 00:02:36,000
P’Sun,

24
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:41,040
you need to live your life.

25
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:16,960
Mom.

26
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,360
P’Sun!

27
00:05:05,560 --> 00:05:06,360
P’Sun!

28
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,440
P’Sun!

29
00:05:08,640 --> 00:05:10,000
Are you awake?

30
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:11,760
P’Sun, do you remember me?

31
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,720
I’m the person that you really adore, remember?

32
00:05:14,560 --> 00:05:15,400
Sun!

33
00:05:23,880 --> 00:05:25,200
Do you remember us?

34
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:26,600
Who am I?

35
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:35,720
My Manager.

36
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,040
You've been sleeping for weeks,

37
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,480
even though the surgery went well.

38
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,520
We're so very worried.

39
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,680
I’m so thankful for you that day.

40
00:05:56,560 --> 00:05:57,840
If it wasn’t for you that save me,

41
00:05:58,480 --> 00:05:59,120
I would…

42
00:05:59,120 --> 00:05:59,680
You won’t.

43
00:06:05,640 --> 00:06:06,240
Really,

44
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:08,960
everything that happened.

45
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:12,320
It came out of my own resentment.

46
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:15,920
Okay,

47
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:19,560
The fact that you survived is beyond good news.

48
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:24,440
Next time, don't do this again. I'm begging you.

49
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,280
Sky, can you put the bed upward?

50
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:50,840
You okay?

51
00:06:57,280 --> 00:06:58,000
Alright?

52
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:19,800
TWO-O

53
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:22,040
has anyone heard about him?

54
00:07:26,360 --> 00:07:27,280
Not yet.

55
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,200
Here you go!

56
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,240
You used to love this, didn't you?

57
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:40,720
P’Pong?

58
00:07:45,440 --> 00:07:46,720
You can eat this

59
00:07:47,480 --> 00:07:48,480
when you get better, alright?

60
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,560
Hey!

61
00:07:54,800 --> 00:07:55,840
Let go.

62
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:04,520
Let go of it!

63
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,120
How did you even come?

64
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:29,920
Oh here, I’m representing Speed Express.

65
00:08:32,919 --> 00:08:33,640
Before this,

66
00:08:34,320 --> 00:08:37,240
when you were taking other people's shifts to help them,

67
00:08:38,240 --> 00:08:39,440
it meant a lot to them.

68
00:08:41,200 --> 00:08:42,240
But of course, you didn’t know that, right?

69
00:08:45,360 --> 00:08:48,560
I didn't think it would matter to anyone.

70
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:51,960
It’s fine. It’s good that you’re awake.

71
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:52,800
Here.

72
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,800
These are your friends.

73
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:57,120
They pitched in to get these for you.

74
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,840
You have to eat it all.

75
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:04,000
And be careful of others, they might steal it.

76
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:05,600
Oh, hey!

77
00:09:07,120 --> 00:09:09,560
Right, I'll head back first.

78
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:11,640
I will deliver them the good news that you’re awake.

79
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:13,000
I'll put it here.

80
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:14,760
Thank you.

81
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,560
Eat it all, okay?

82
00:09:19,360 --> 00:09:21,360
You two better be careful!
I’m keeping both of my eyes on you.

83
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:23,920
What!?

84
00:09:24,560 --> 00:09:25,360
What a crazy man!

85
00:09:26,520 --> 00:09:27,360
Hey.

86
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:33,760
Who is this again?

87
00:09:38,560 --> 00:09:39,520
I'm sorry,

88
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:41,200
but I think you came to the wrong room.

89
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,000
Oh, hi, uncle.

90
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:47,520
Sia?

91
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:51,360
Oh, this uncle is

92
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,760
the person who helped me when Sun passed out.

93
00:09:58,480 --> 00:09:59,240
Thank you so much.

94
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:01,760
Since you two seem to know each other so well.

95
00:10:02,880 --> 00:10:06,640
I’ll let you two be.

96
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,760
We should go eat.

97
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,000
Take care, alright?

98
00:10:15,560 --> 00:10:16,360
Let’s go.

99
00:10:22,360 --> 00:10:23,760
Wait up, Mr. Manager.

100
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:31,320
If you ever need someone for a male lead,

101
00:10:33,520 --> 00:10:34,480
do not hesitate to call me, okay?

102
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,720
Why the heck would you sit up?

103
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:05,920
Didn’t you look that they nearly stabbed your gut out,

104
00:11:06,360 --> 00:11:07,400
and you’re still acting tough?

105
00:11:09,440 --> 00:11:10,600
How did you come?

106
00:11:11,640 --> 00:11:14,120
Sia Jo, he called me.

107
00:11:14,480 --> 00:11:15,840
He said that you might be in trouble.

108
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,680
Although I didn't believe him.

109
00:11:18,720 --> 00:11:20,600
So I went to see it with my very own eyes.

110
00:11:22,560 --> 00:11:23,560
Sia Jo from Alice?

111
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:26,440
That's right.

112
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:27,720
Sia Jo,

113
00:11:27,920 --> 00:11:31,280
or that bastard from Alice is my pal.

114
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,880
We’re tight.

115
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:34,000
When we were younger,

116
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:35,200
we've been to bathhouses together,

117
00:11:35,600 --> 00:11:36,440
but now

118
00:11:36,720 --> 00:11:37,880
it looks like he has his own bathhouse now.

119
00:11:39,480 --> 00:11:39,920
Confused?

120
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:44,920
He also used to call,

121
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,520
and fact check your story with me.

122
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,240
And after he knew

123
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,680
that you had to work your ass off to pay my debt,

124
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:53,920
he cried like an old looking freaking baby.

125
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:55,400
I don't know what the hell is wrong with him.

126
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,240
That bastard likes to act all dramatic.

127
00:12:05,120 --> 00:12:08,840
So, I owe you again?

128
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,760
This one you didn’t ask for.

129
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,760
And I'm willing to help

130
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:17,360
so I don't count.

131
00:12:21,760 --> 00:12:22,760
Thank you.

132
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:26,880
And when I passed out,

133
00:12:28,240 --> 00:12:29,240
what happened?

134
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:48,160
Who are you?

135
00:12:50,600 --> 00:12:52,600
Don't you remember your daddy's face, boy?

136
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:54,880
Finish him!

137
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:04,560
Hey!

138
00:13:05,560 --> 00:13:06,680
Are you really in trouble?

139
00:13:14,800 --> 00:13:15,600
And you?

140
00:13:19,040 --> 00:13:21,240
Oh, you still look fine.

141
00:13:22,120 --> 00:13:23,760
Looks like I still have time for something fun.

142
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,440
Beat the shit out of him!

143
00:14:33,680 --> 00:14:34,760
Since when did you come back?

144
00:14:44,200 --> 00:14:44,920
Are you angry?

145
00:14:57,480 --> 00:14:58,640
The suicide scene,

146
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:01,840
now I get it.

147
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,560
Why you portrayed the scene that way.

148
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,400
What do you mean?

149
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,480
You put your life at risk,

150
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,840
even though I told you to only focus on yourself.

151
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:20,080
Thirty missed calls from me.

152
00:15:21,280 --> 00:15:22,400
You didn’t answer my calls at all.

153
00:15:24,720 --> 00:15:26,720
If you have to choose between death and me,

154
00:15:28,560 --> 00:15:29,960
you would choose death without any hesitation, right?

155
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:33,160
I don't…

156
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:33,920
You feel guilty.

157
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,120
because you blamed yourself for your brother's
and mother's deaths.

158
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:57,760
Jay.

159
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:00,960
Jay!

160
00:16:03,480 --> 00:16:04,640
Put the knife down!

161
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:07,080
We can talk.

162
00:16:12,120 --> 00:16:13,000
Jay.

163
00:16:13,480 --> 00:16:13,960
Jay.

164
00:16:13,960 --> 00:16:14,560
Jay, don’t.

165
00:16:14,760 --> 00:16:15,280
No.

166
00:16:15,280 --> 00:16:16,280
Jay, please.

167
00:16:19,240 --> 00:16:20,360
Jay, don't.

168
00:16:20,360 --> 00:16:21,160
Jay.

169
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:26,400
No, Jay.

170
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:27,520
Jay!

171
00:16:27,800 --> 00:16:28,440
Jay, stop!

172
00:16:29,360 --> 00:16:29,960
Jay!

173
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:00,880
How do you feel now

174
00:17:03,520 --> 00:17:04,680
to be the one who’s trying to kill me?

175
00:17:32,120 --> 00:17:33,080
I'm sorry.

176
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,000
I'm really sorry.

177
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,440
Ahh.

178
00:18:46,520 --> 00:18:47,520
Two baht guy,

179
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,720
you’re looking for my Jay, right?

180
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:54,160
That guy has something to deal with.

181
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,120
The injury isn't serious.

182
00:18:57,560 --> 00:18:58,600
so the doctor let him go since he’s quite stable.

183
00:19:01,520 --> 00:19:04,240
Although the doctor referred him
to the psychiatric department

184
00:19:04,960 --> 00:19:06,520
because they thought that he tried to kill himself.

185
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,200
So I told the doctor,

186
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:09,920
“Doctor, sir.

187
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:11,920
he only did that to get back at his boyfriend”

188
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:15,680
But the doctor insisted that he should be
cleared by a psychiatrist anyway.

189
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,920
He really needs a good therapist anyway.

190
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:30,080
You say nothing about the fact that
I call you his boyfriend,

191
00:19:31,120 --> 00:19:32,480
so you…

192
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:35,320
are really becoming Mr. Three baht?

193
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:35,640
Huh?

194
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:36,400
Right?

195
00:19:36,480 --> 00:19:36,880
Huh?

196
00:19:37,200 --> 00:19:37,920
Mr. Three baht

197
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:38,760
Mr. Three baht

198
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:39,840
Mr. Three baht

199
00:19:40,360 --> 00:19:41,840
Hoo! Hoo! Hoo!

200
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:45,400
It’s not like that.

201
00:19:49,360 --> 00:19:50,400
Whatever,

202
00:19:55,360 --> 00:19:58,120
I'm sorry for my beloved nephew.

203
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:02,760
Sometimes he likes to be self-centered like a child.

204
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,920
But after this,

205
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:09,440
I need you to control his behavior.

206
00:20:10,800 --> 00:20:11,200
I think…

207
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,760
You can do it, right?

208
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:14,400
Huh?

209
00:20:15,520 --> 00:20:17,160
Good, good.

210
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,560
I'm glad that

211
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:23,080
you're not dead.

212
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,440
You're Mr. Three Baht.

213
00:20:29,680 --> 00:20:31,360
That means you're family.

214
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:35,640
Family

215
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,360
needs to rely on each other.

216
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,640
You stay here.

217
00:20:58,520 --> 00:20:59,360
I have to go.

218
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:12,160
Please take care of him for me.

219
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:13,960
Yes.

220
00:21:29,440 --> 00:21:31,440
You didn’t have to lie to me.

221
00:21:34,600 --> 00:21:35,160
I…

222
00:21:35,200 --> 00:21:37,520
You want me to feel even more guilty?

223
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:45,760
Let’s go back to your room.

224
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:56,160
You’re invited to the meeting. Click the link below to join.

225
00:22:06,640 --> 00:22:07,360
Hello, all of you.

226
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:08,040
Hello, sir.

227
00:22:08,080 --> 00:22:09,160
Sit down, sit down, please.

228
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:12,880
Thank you so much.

229
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:17,280
Sorry to keep you all waiting.

230
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:19,280
We can start now.

231
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:23,240
Alright, I’m going to cut to the chase now.

232
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:26,000
Our company

233
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:30,120
has improved significantly over the past several years.

234
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:34,800
We are now the leading entertainment company in the country.

235
00:22:37,920 --> 00:22:40,920
Even though what we still lack now is funding.

236
00:22:42,760 --> 00:22:46,080
And that is the reason why Mr.Songpol is here with us today.

237
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:52,480
The chairman and the board members

238
00:22:52,520 --> 00:22:54,320
have proposed a merger of the company.

239
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:57,120
Between Dream Entertainment and SPG

240
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:00,680
where the SPG will be a major investor.

241
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:02,880
They will increase the capital by three times

242
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:05,000
the company's market capitalization.

243
00:23:06,040 --> 00:23:07,520
And we also would like to propose a name
change of the company to

244
00:23:07,680 --> 00:23:10,160
SPDream for our unity.

245
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:13,480
It sounds good.

246
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:15,360
But why is it so sudden?

247
00:23:15,480 --> 00:23:16,640
It's not sudden at all.

248
00:23:17,320 --> 00:23:20,080
All propose is for the future of SPDream

249
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,760
which will grow to be the leader

250
00:23:23,520 --> 00:23:25,040
in the industry globally.

251
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:26,280
Besides,

252
00:23:26,560 --> 00:23:29,120
the board members demanded the removal of Director Arthur

253
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:30,920
from Dream Entertainment.

254
00:23:34,840 --> 00:23:36,160
As you all know,

255
00:23:37,680 --> 00:23:39,680
Director Arthur actions,

256
00:23:40,240 --> 00:23:41,600
what he has done without consulting others.

257
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:44,360
His action has damaged the company gravely.

258
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:49,400
Yeah, he ruined many good deals that I've made.

259
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:53,200
And also his arrogant demeanor

260
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,880
has given the company bad publicity.

261
00:23:57,240 --> 00:23:58,360
Not to mention that

262
00:23:59,160 --> 00:24:01,160
he just signed off on tens of millions Baht

263
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,400
to approve that unknown indie woman director

264
00:24:03,800 --> 00:24:05,200
on a random project.

265
00:24:05,760 --> 00:24:06,520
You’re right.

266
00:24:10,520 --> 00:24:12,360
I understand everyone's frustration,

267
00:24:12,760 --> 00:24:15,440
so should we vote now?

268
00:24:19,920 --> 00:24:20,800
Who will vote to dismiss him from the position?

269
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:45,720
Are you trying to fire me?

270
00:25:03,400 --> 00:25:07,040
Sometimes Jay still has a mischievous side.

271
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:08,960
Have a look at this.

272
00:25:21,040 --> 00:25:23,240
How did you know Jay?

273
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,520
I was a bodyguard for Jay's mother.

274
00:25:38,360 --> 00:25:40,760
I had worked with her for the longest time.

275
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:44,880
I made a mistake that day.

276
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:47,320
Yes?

277
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:51,160
A parcel for Ms. Pavinee?

278
00:26:00,400 --> 00:26:01,200
Yes, yes.

279
00:26:27,480 --> 00:26:30,160
I only let you out of my sight for a second.

280
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:31,200
What!

281
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:34,600
No, what is happening to her?

282
00:26:40,800 --> 00:26:41,600
Boss!

283
00:26:43,000 --> 00:26:43,800
Boss!

284
00:26:44,440 --> 00:26:45,160
Miss Pavinee!

285
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:08,240
Jay and I met again at his mother's funeral.

286
